,"_gate_spread":-0.05604486313094243,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.4665884796758424,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":22.2,"_gate_incr_roic":0.033487637903349035,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":27.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.07281988750072349,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":57.6,"_gate_pool_share":0.6220821544315525,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.5385174880399894,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.050305206580908285,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.23222775175085464,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.030245223223900802,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":49.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.0051200003,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"NETSTREIT Corp. is an internally managed real estate investment trust based in Dallas, Texas that specializes in acquiring single-tenant net lease retail properties nationwide. The growing portfolio consists of high-quality properties leased to e-commerce resistant tenants with healthy balance sheets. Led by a management team of seasoned commercial real estate executives, NETSTREIT's strategy is to create the highest quality net lease retail portfolio in the country with the goal of generating consistent cash flows and dividends for its investors. NETSTREIT Corp. was incorporated in 2019 in Maryland and is based in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark  Manheimer | President, CEO, Secretary & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 29 people. Revenue per employee of $6.7M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 27%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $3.8M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $203K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["NetSTREIT Corp. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $2.3B market cap on $195M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +27% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $109M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 56 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 15.87\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 5.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 68/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 61% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"NETSTREIT Corp. $NTST Stock Acquired by Jefferies Financial Group Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/netstreit-corp-ntst-stock-acquired-by-jefferies-financial-group-inc.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794560710.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the NTST Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily